**Read:** [Principles of Extractive Metallurgy — Tarun Kumar Kundu, NPTEL](../sources/Principles-of-Extractive-Metallurgy-NPTEL.lingua#r_7VCNEHN5VCQDDQTZ512PSHFZ78), the opening overview first, followed by the entire public course; [Phase Transitions — Bhadeshia and Yan](../sources/Phase-Transitions-Bhadeshia-Yan.lingua#r_2PMPJ2B4GPGDT62S567TX1DCPJ), the whole book as concepts arise; [Materials, energy, and heat balances in metallurgical processes — Satish Ch. Koria](../sources/Metallurgical-Material-and-Heat-Balances-NPTEL.lingua#r_38NWQRDJH3RVM3NNGB71RR1X43), the full web course and worked video progression.

Begin with the next object/material question and the opening extraction-course overview. Read the entire Phase Transitions book as its concepts develop, and complete the material/heat-balance web progression with worked video explanations. Use [Quantitative and technical literacy](../../../inquiry/quantitative-literacy/Quantitative-literacy.lingua#r_4XVN56PQC13JGNFPV0CSGXDCZ2), [General chemistry](../../../chemistry/general-chemistry/General-chemistry.lingua#r_206GS6CVXD8WSY1VX7PRF7136V), [Measurement and metrology](../../../inquiry/metrology/Metrology.lingua#r_3G54ENPA974K19AB5XF0P641N5), [Mineralogy and petrology — minerals, crystals, rock processes, and investigation](../../../../gaia/earth/mineralogy-and-petrology/Mineralogy-and-petrology.lingua#r_44F7X6GPMW6ZSCCN6D71QSVKBN), and [Mining and mineral engineering — extraction, processing, and continuing work](../../../engineering/mining-and-mineral-engineering/Mining-and-mineral-engineering.lingua#r_22HJPS3RTK5EX1J55YJP75PHYA) where an idea is unfamiliar; their full programmes remain available without making every neighboring field an entry requirement.

Complete the full public extraction/nonferrous and iron/steel course sequences during the process and metal-family Records. Whole corresponding technical chapters and complete cases supply industrial context. English and Portuguese sources can be used together. Compare definitions, phase/chemical models, balances, rates, equipment/utility systems, product specification, and residual/recovery work on consistent boundaries.

Complete the published Cambridge metals/alloys and master-level steel exercises, MIT processing course, and forming/powder/practical public sequences as structure and manufacturing deepen. Read the whole advanced transformation books and solidification guide. The later graduate mechanics programme, complete primary computational papers, NIST guides, full technical methods, and independent projects demand progressively stronger derivation, observation, comparison, and validation.

[Complete substantial metallurgical books, university work, and connected process cases](../research/A-sustained-metallurgical-theory-and-practice-programme.lingua#r_1SHGMZ8VHVSK4XT13EPK5P2EEJ) names the sustained books/course work; [Metals and metallurgical production sources — books, courses, methods, and cases](../Sources.lingua#r_03Z21BSG78ZRQSAVCCD6FJVNRY) identifies actual editions, rights, access, and inspection limits. Specific later readings can narrow to an equation, method, specimen population, or chapter section after the complete work provides context. All books, articles, datasets, standards, software, and media remain externally referenced. These Records supply original explanations, examples, demanding work, and ordinary connections through the shared body of knowledge.

